  "summary": "Suffolk County lawmakers questioned Flock Safety representatives at a Public Safety Committee hearing about privacy, data access, and potential misuse of the company's license plate readers, which are used by SCPD, the sheriff's office, and East End agencies. Flock defended the technology as a law enforcement tool with audit logs, while legislators suggested additional safeguards may be needed. Separately, the county recently paused a proposed $4 million Flock gunshot detection contract.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Isn't it true you've constructed a nationwide surveillance network capable of reconstructing an individual's movements over time?",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "The courts have found it's not a surveillance tool that can track a person's course of daily life.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "If someone here were to do like has been reported in other places in the country and run their boyfriend or girlfriend a thousand times, they're going to go to jail",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Suffolk County officials recently paused plans to move forward with a proposed $4 million agreement with Flock Safety for gunshot detection technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
